                    "Instead of thinking about the entire syllabus, "
                    "pick one subject and one small topic. Give it "
                    "your full attention for the next 20–30 minutes. "
                    "Then decide what comes next. 🌱\n\n"

                    "You don't need to prove that you can finish "
                    "everything tonight. You only need to make the "
                    "next bit of progress.\n\n"

                    "Which subject is worrying you the most right now?"
                )
            }


        if (
            "tired" in lower_text
            or "exhausted" in lower_text
            or "can't focus" in lower_text
            or "cannot focus" in lower_text
        ):

            return {
                "reply": (
                    "🌱 It sounds like you're mentally exhausted, not "
                    "just busy. When your brain has been thinking about "
                    "deadlines for too long, even starting can feel "
                    "like a huge task.\n\n"

                    "Don't try to force yourself through everything at "
                    "once. Take a short break, drink some water, and "
                    "come back with one very small task.\n\n"

                    "You don't need a perfect study session. Even a "
                    "small amount of focused work counts. 💜\n\n"

                    "What is the easiest thing you could start with?"
                )
            }


        return {
            "reply": (
                "🌱 It sounds like academics are taking up a lot of "
                "space in your mind right now.\n\n"

                "Try not to measure your progress against everyone "
                "else. People rarely show how much they are struggling "
                "behind the scenes.\n\n"

                "Focus on your own list: what needs to be done first, "
                "what can wait, and what can realistically be finished "
                "today.\n\n"

                "You don't have to finish everything perfectly. "
                "You just need to keep moving forward. 💜\n\n"

                "What are you working on at the moment?"
            )
        }


    # =========================================================
    # ANGER
    # =========================================================

    anger_words = [
        "angry",
        "anger",
        "furious",
        "frustrated",
        "frustrating",
        "annoyed",
        "annoying",
        "pissed",
        "mad",
        "rage",
        "irritated"
    ]

    if any(word in lower_text for word in anger_words):

        if (
            "lie" in lower_text
            or "lied" in lower_text
            or "lying" in lower_text
            or "trust" in lower_text
            or "betray" in lower_text
            or "betrayed" in lower_text
        ):

            return {
                "reply": (
                    "🫂 I can understand why you're angry. When "
                    "someone you trusted lies to you, the anger often "
